  "implementation": {
    "protocol": "48-byte v2 request retains the v1 prefix; bounded primary/secondary paths, explicit permissions/umask/size, no client-supplied UID/native provider inode/handle. Fstat/ftruncate require exactly one transferred SCM_RIGHTS descriptor. All received descriptors are closed on every path, including fragmented headers and truncated/excess ancillary data.",
    "identity": "Kernel SO_PEERCRED plus peer thread-group membership and live PID/start-time record. The trusted embedding service can select a profile identity-record directory; that path is not accepted in the app protocol. Logical guest identity is not an independent kernel security boundary.",
    "descriptorProof": "Only authenticated Manager attach establishes proxy device/inode to an active slot/cookie. Application FD operations validate the received kernel descriptor against that binding. Unbound files, absent/extra rights, stale caps and foreign threads/processes are rejected. Native UID0 broker inspects real kernel proxy metadata to avoid recursive dispatch.",
    "operations": "Open/create with original flags and explicit mode/mask, fresh path/fd attrs, mkdir, unlink/rmdir, two-path rename, path/fd truncate, and provider access checks. Provider errors propagate. Existing v1 regular-file protocol remains supported. Directory FD attachment is explicitly rejected until a directory transport exists.",
    "loader": "Additional namespace marker gates dispatch, without enabling it in normal Manager. Maps regular-file fstat and ftruncate using actual proxy FD proofs; maps fstatat/AT_EMPTY_PATH, mkdirat, unlinkat, renameat/renameat2, truncate and faccessat through the broker. Unsupported external path operations fail instead of mutating the lower tree. Cross-mount rename is rejected.",
    "creation": "Original paths may not exist. Alias and relative-dirfd resolution can recover a missing child from its parent/base directory. Umask is read from proc status without changing the process-wide mask.",
    "metadata": "Wire attributes populate native stat, so path/fd device, inode and size match provider values instead of exposing the AppFuse slot as a guest inode. The broker keeps no dentry/attribute cache."
  },
